# 0009. Jupyter notebooks: jupytext, molten and image.nvim

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-07

Notebooks open as plain Python with `# %%` cells, run in a real Jupyter kernel and show
plots in the terminal.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: `.ipynb` files should open, run and be edited in Neovim with normal Python
  tooling (pyright, completion, formatting).
- **jupytext.nvim** (`lua/plugins/notebook.lua`): `style = "percent"`,
  `output_extension = "auto"`; converts the notebook to a script on read and writes it back
  on save, outputs kept. `lazy = false` because it owns `BufReadCmd *.ipynb`; setup only
  registers the autocmd, so start cost is nil. The jupytext CLI comes from
  `uv tool install jupytext`.
- **molten-nvim** (`version = "^1.0.0"`, `build = ":UpdateRemotePlugins"`): runs cells in a
  Jupyter kernel; outputs as virtual text under each cell (max 20 lines), float only on
  `\jo`, tick rate 150 ms. No `cmd` lazy trigger: its commands come from the remote-plugin
  manifest and lazy's stand-ins would replace them.
- **image.nvim**: `backend = "kitty"` (Ghostty speaks the kitty graphics protocol),
  `processor = "magick_cli"`, only molten draws images (markdown and other integrations
  off), max 100x20, hidden under floats. Inside tmux it needs `allow-passthrough on`.
- **Python host**: `make notebook` creates `~/.local/share/nvim/python-host` with
  `uv venv --python 3.12` and installs `pynvim`, `jupyter_client`, `nbformat`, `pillow`;
  `options.lua` sets `python3_host_prog` to it (else the provider is off). Ruby, Perl and
  Node providers are disabled. `make kernel VENV=path/.venv [NAME=...]` installs `ipykernel`
  in a project venv and registers it.
- **Cells** (`lua/config/notebook.lua`): a cell is the text between two `<comment> %%` lines
  (comment leader from `commentstring`, so `// %%` in Go); `[markdown]`/`[raw]` cells are
  skipped when running; a file without markers is one cell. Kernel choice: the one saved in
  the notebook, else the one registered for the project's `.venv`, else a list.
- **Keys** under `\j`: `ji` start kernel, `jr` run cell (visual: selection), `jn` run and
  next, `ja`/`jA`/`jb` all/above/below, `jl` line, `jo`/`jh` output, `jd`/`jD` delete
  outputs, `jx` interrupt, `jR` restart, `jp` plot popup, `jc`/`jm` new code/markdown cell;
  `]j`/`[j` move between cells.
- **Consequences**: the notebook is plain Python in the buffer, so all tooling works
  unchanged. Needs `uv`, a python host per machine, ImageMagick, and tmux passthrough for
  images.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: jupytext.nvim + jupytext CLI, molten-nvim, image.nvim, Jupyter
  (`jupyter_client`, `ipykernel`), pynvim, uv, ImageMagick, kitty graphics protocol.
